## Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Senkai project.

### Changes Made:

1. **Installed Package:**
   - Added `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 to project dependencies
   - Used npm to install the package as per project's package manager

2. **Modified Files:**
   - `src/app/layout.js` - Added Analytics component following Next.js App Router pattern
     - Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next"`
     - Placed `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag, after the ThemeProvider wrapper
     
3. **Updated Lock Files:**
   - `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics to dependencies
   - `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and its dependencies

### Implementation Details:

The implementation follows the official Vercel Analytics documentation for Next.js App Router:
- Fetched latest installation instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Used the framework-specific approach for Next.js App Router
- Analytics component placed at the end of the body tag to avoid blocking page rendering
- Preserves all existing code structure including ClerkProvider, ThemeProvider, and font configurations

### Verification:

- ✅ Build completed successfully without errors
- ✅ Linter executed (pre-existing errors in other files, none introduced by Analytics)
- ✅ Lock files properly updated
- ✅ All changes are source code only (no build artifacts)

### Next Steps:

To activate analytics:
1. Deploy the project to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard under Analytics
3. Verify analytics are working by checking browser Network tab for requests to the analytics endpoint

The Analytics component will automatically collect page view data and send it to Vercel once the project is deployed and analytics are enabled in the dashboard.
